### @TimeTracker  ->  TimeTrackerAspect (@Around), on CRUDBookServiceImpl#updateBookDetails.
### Like @Auditable, the effect is log-only. Triggering the PATCH below should print:
###
###   Starting timeTracker for method: CRUDBookServiceImpl.updateBookDetails(..)
###   Method has finished its execution: CRUDBookServiceImpl.updateBookDetails(..), timeMs: <n>
###
### NOTE: the aspect reads stopWatch.getTotalTimeMillis() without calling stopWatch.stop(),
### so <n> currently prints as 0. The @Around advice itself still fires correctly.
### updateBookDetails requires ADMIN, so we log in as admin and create a book to update.

### login admin
POST http://localhost:8080/realms/uni-book-store/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=uni-book-store-client&username=admin&password=admin

> {% client.global.set("admin_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### create a book to update (so the PATCH has a valid, existing id)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/v1/books
Authorization: Bearer {{admin_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Timed Book",
  "description": "Will be updated to trigger @TimeTracker",
  "author": "Author",
  "genre": "ADVENTURE",
  "imageUrl": "https://example.com/timed.jpg",
  "enabled": true,
  "price": 18.00,
  "quantity": 4
}

> {%
    client.test("book created", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "Expected 201 but got " + response.status);
    });
    client.global.set("timed_book_id", response.body.id);
%}

### updateBookDetails -> @Around @TimeTracker fires, expect 200 + two timeTracker log lines
PATCH http://localhost:8081/api/v1/books/{{timed_book_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Updated - watch the timeTracker start/finish log lines"
}

> {%
    client.test("updateBookDetails returns 200 (timeTracker lines expected in logs)", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}
